From bb1aa2cf90a5210359a74edb23254c2d0883b5a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LiBr <me@nvme0n1p.dev>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 05:47:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/57] Z 6III: the body's buttons -- the MCU's I2C expanders
 answer, and MENU opens

With mcu-image= the body MCU builds the key report itself (family 2 kind
1, sub_8043C2C; the EXPEED's sub_41011850 names its bytes), and it read
every button held. Most buttons are behind two devices on FMPI2C1, 0x22
and 0x23: the switch service reads each one's three input ports
(sub_80352C4 -> sub_8034800: 8-bit addresses 0x44 and 0x46, register 0,
three bytes, table 0x80583c8) and takes a button as pressed when its bit
is 0 (sub_803D998 / sub_803DA14: ~input & mask). As a plain register
file both read 0 -- MENU, PLAY, OK, the multi-selector, the
sub-selector, DISP, i, DELETE, zoom, Fn, the movie-record button, all
held for ever. They now answer their input ports from levels, 1 =
released unless the board presses one: the input port of a 24-bit I/O
expander of the TCA6424A kind, whose two addresses these are. DECLARED:
released = 1; the part is not identified.

At run time the expander task ("IoExpCyc", sub_8034D18) reads both every
~12 ms and hands the bytes to the key task (sub_80449F4 -> sub_8044960),
so no interrupt line is needed. Which MCU pins the parts' INT outputs
reach is not known, and the two tried were worse than none: PC7 is a
shutter position sensor (asserting it made the shutter report status 6
and the camera post error 0x39), and EXTI7 on PG7 resets the MCU. INT is
not modelled.

Those polled reads are interrupt-driven, and FMPI2C1 raised only NACK and
STOP: a read began and never finished, so the input buffer at 0x20019e04
never changed (found by watching it with z63watch). The event line now
also follows TXIE/TXIS, RXIE/RXNE and TCIE with TC or TCR, and is
re-evaluated after an RXDR read.

hw/arm/nikon-z63-mcukeys.h names the buttons: the expander bits through
the key task's run-time tables (0x80578d6 for 0x23: MENU is bit 6, key
byte 37, report byte 0x43; 0x22's names are the power-on path's and not
yet checked against 0x80578be), plus the GPIO ones from the MCU's pin
tables (shutter half PG1, full PG13, AF-ON PG2, ISO PC2), which now idle
released along with the 10-pin remote's inputs. -machine mcu-keys=,
qom-set /machine mcu-keys (':'-separated, empty releases all) and the
display window's keyboard press them; mcu-pins= still overrides a pin.

Verified, with the SNOR_USER body's sensor tables emptied: the camera
comes up in photo mode with nothing held; shutter half and full press
produce key reports; MENU opens the setup menu; down moves the
selection, left goes to the tab column, up to the playback menu, right
enters it.

Where it stands: a half press to leave the menu restarts live view, and
the restart ends in camera error 0x35 or 0x40, varying from run to run.
At boot the camera says the memory card cannot be accessed.

